<h2>How Parameters Connect to Actions</h2>

<p>
    Every action (such as sending an email) uses parameters to fill in its fields. When you set up an action, you map each field to a parameter.
</p>

<p>
    For example, a "Send renewal reminder" agent might map:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Client</strong> parameter → Email greeting ("Dear [Client Name]") and subject line</li>
    <li><strong>Policy</strong> parameter → Policy details in the body of the email</li>
    <li><strong>Contact Email</strong> parameter → "To" field in the Outlook template</li>
    <li><strong>Due Date</strong> parameter → A line in the message reminding the client when to respond</li>
</ul>

<p>
    When the agent runs, the system takes the parameter values and plugs them into the corresponding fields in your email template or action.
</p>

