<h2>Cleaning Up and Iterating</h2>

<p>
    As you use agents, you'll learn what works and what doesn't:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Remove unused parameters</strong> – If an agent has become complicated, remove parameters that are no longer used and simplify the form</li>
    <li><strong>Test from real pages</strong> – Test the agent from a real page to confirm that parameters are pulled from context correctly</li>
    <li><strong>Adjust based on usage</strong> – As you learn how teammates use the agent, adjust parameter names and defaults to make it faster and more obvious</li>
    <li><strong>Make required parameters hidden</strong> – If a parameter is always available from the page, make it hidden to simplify the interface</li>
    <li><strong>Add helpful descriptions</strong> – Add tooltips or descriptions to parameters to explain what they're for</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Before-and-after example showing a long parameter list simplified into a smaller, clearer set of required fields. Show how the run dialog becomes cleaner and easier to use. -->

<h2>Best Practices</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Keep it simple</strong> – Only ask for information you actually need</li>
    <li><strong>Use hidden parameters</strong> – Pull data from the page automatically when possible</li>
    <li><strong>Set helpful defaults</strong> – Pre-fill common values to save users time</li>
    <li><strong>Name clearly</strong> – Use descriptive parameter names that explain what's needed</li>
    <li><strong>Make required obvious</strong> – Clearly mark which parameters are required</li>
    <li><strong>Test thoroughly</strong> – Verify that parameters pull the right data in different contexts</li>
    <li><strong>Iterate based on feedback</strong> – Adjust parameters as you learn how agents are actually used</li>
</ul>

